1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,690
Section 1

2
00:00:02,690 --> 00:00:03,234
MAN:

3
00:00:03,234 --> 00:00:05,730
Good morning, Kenton Festival box office.

4
00:00:05,730 --> 00:00:07,140
How can I help you?

5
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:07,190
WOMAN:

6
00:00:07,190 --> 00:00:08,643
Oh, good morning.

7
00:00:08,643 --> 00:00:12,776
I'm coming to Kenton for a few days' holiday next month,

8
00:00:12,776 --> 00:00:15,782
and a friend told me there's a festival.

9
00:00:15,782 --> 00:00:19,540
She gave me this number to find out about it.

10
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:19,972
MAN:

11
00:00:19,972 --> 00:00:24,289
That's right, the festival begins on the 16th of May

12
00:00:24,289 --> 00:00:26,880
and goes on till the 19th.

13
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:27,295
WOMAN:

14
00:00:27,295 --> 00:00:27,710
Oh,

15
00:00:27,710 --> 00:00:28,539
that's great.

16
00:00:28,539 --> 00:00:32,272
I'll be there from the 15th till the 19th.

17
00:00:32,272 --> 00:00:35,590
So could you tell me the programme, please?

18
00:00:35,590 --> 00:00:36,050
MAN:

19
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:42,033
Well, on the first day, there's the opening ceremony, in the town centre.

20
00:00:42,033 --> 00:00:48,477
People start gathering around 2 o'clock, to get a good place to see from,

21
00:00:48,477 --> 00:00:52,159
and the events will start at 2.45,

22
00:00:52,159 --> 00:00:54,460
and finish about 5.30.

23
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:54,814
WOMAN:

24
00:00:54,814 --> 00:00:55,522
OK, thanks.

25
00:00:55,522 --> 00:00:59,770
I'll make sure I get there early to get a good spot.

26
00:00:59,770 --> 00:01:00,204
MAN:

27
00:01:00,204 --> 00:01:04,114
The festival will be officially opened by the mayor.

28
00:01:04,114 --> 00:01:09,328
He'll just speak for a few minutes, welcoming everyone to the festival.

29
00:01:09,328 --> 00:01:12,369
All the town councillors will be there,

30
00:01:12,369 --> 00:01:15,410
and of course lots of other people.

31
00:01:15,410 --> 00:01:16,260
WOMAN:

32
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:17,110
Right.

33
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:17,549
MAN:

34
00:01:17,549 --> 00:01:21,058
Then there'll be a performance by a band.

35
00:01:21,058 --> 00:01:24,129
Most years we have a children's choir,

36
00:01:24,129 --> 00:01:28,515
but this year the local army cadets offered to perform,

37
00:01:28,515 --> 00:01:30,270
and they're very good.

38
00:01:30,270 --> 00:01:30,985
WOMAN:

39
00:01:30,985 --> 00:01:31,700
Uhuh.

40
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:32,127
MAN:

41
00:01:32,127 --> 00:01:38,103
After that, a community group from the town will perform a play they've written

42
00:01:38,103 --> 00:01:40,238
themselves, just a short one.

43
00:01:40,238 --> 00:01:41,945
It's about Helen Tungate.

44
00:01:41,945 --> 00:01:45,360
I don't know if you've heard of her?

45
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:45,872
WOMAN:

46
00:01:45,872 --> 00:01:47,408
I certainly have.

47
00:01:47,408 --> 00:01:50,480
She was a scientist years ago.

48
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:51,004
MAN:

49
00:01:51,004 --> 00:01:52,051
That's right.

50
00:01:52,051 --> 00:01:56,762
She was born in Kenton exactly 100 years ago,

51
00:01:56,762 --> 00:01:59,380
so we're celebrating her centenary.

52
00:01:59,380 --> 00:01:59,782
WOMAN:

53
00:01:59,782 --> 00:02:00,987
I'm a biologist,

54
00:02:00,987 --> 00:02:03,798
so I've always been interested in her.

55
00:02:03,798 --> 00:02:06,610
I didn't realise she came from Kenton.

56
00:02:06,610 --> 00:02:07,022
MAN:

57
00:02:07,022 --> 00:02:07,434
Yes.

58
00:02:07,434 --> 00:02:11,143
Well, all that will take place in the afternoon,

59
00:02:11,143 --> 00:02:15,676
and later, as the sun sets, there'll be a firework display.

60
00:02:15,676 --> 00:02:21,446
You should go to the park to watch, as you'll get the best view

61
00:02:21,446 --> 00:02:22,270
from there.

62
00:02:22,270 --> 00:02:26,642
And the display takes place on the opposite side of the river.

63
00:02:26,642 --> 00:02:30,650
It's always one of the most popular events in the festival.

64
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:31,397
WOMAN:

65
00:02:31,397 --> 00:02:32,890
Sounds great.

66
00:02:32,890 --> 00:02:33,299
WOMAN:

67
00:02:33,299 --> 00:02:36,160
And what's happening on the other days?

68
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:36,624
MAN:

69
00:02:36,624 --> 00:02:41,269
There are several events that go on the whole time.

70
00:02:41,269 --> 00:02:47,770
For example, the students of the art college have produced a number of videos,

71
00:02:47,770 --> 00:02:51,950
all connected with relationships between children and their grandparents.

72
00:02:51,950 --> 00:02:52,417
WOMAN:

73
00:02:52,417 --> 00:02:53,819
That sounds interesting.

74
00:02:53,819 --> 00:02:58,490
It makes a change from children and parents, doesn't it!

75
00:02:58,490 --> 00:02:59,011
MAN:

76
00:02:59,011 --> 00:02:59,533
Exactly.

77
00:02:59,533 --> 00:03:06,832
Because the art college is in use for classes, throughout the festival, the videos

78
00:03:06,832 --> 00:03:09,960
are being shown in Handsworth House.

79
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:10,301
WOMAN:

80
00:03:10,301 --> 00:03:12,350
How do you spell the name?

81
00:03:12,350 --> 00:03:13,585
MAN:

82
00:03:13,585 --> 00:03:14,820
H-A-N-D-S-W-O-R-T-H.

83
00:03:14,820 --> 00:03:17,290
Handsworth House.

84
00:03:17,290 --> 00:03:24,700
It's close to the Town Hall.

85
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:25,375
WOMAN:

86
00:03:25,375 --> 00:03:26,050
Right.

87
00:03:26,050 --> 00:03:26,462
MAN:

88
00:03:26,462 --> 00:03:31,000
Now let me see, what else can I tell you about?

89
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:31,384
WOMAN:

90
00:03:31,384 --> 00:03:34,068
Are there any displays of ballet dancing?

91
00:03:34,068 --> 00:03:38,670
I'm particularly interested in that as I do it as a hobby.

92
00:03:38,670 --> 00:03:39,108
MAN:

93
00:03:39,108 --> 00:03:41,736
There isn't any ballet, I'm afraid,

94
00:03:41,736 --> 00:03:47,430
but there'll be a demonstration of traditional dances from all round the country.

95
00:03:47,430 --> 00:03:47,873
WOMAN:

96
00:03:47,873 --> 00:03:48,317
Oh,

97
00:03:48,317 --> 00:03:49,647
that'd be nice.

98
00:03:49,647 --> 00:03:51,420
Where's that being held?

99
00:03:51,420 --> 00:03:51,862
MAN:

100
00:03:51,862 --> 00:03:57,601
It's in the market in the town centre - the outdoor one, not the

101
00:03:57,601 --> 00:03:58,484
covered market.

102
00:03:58,484 --> 00:04:04,665
And it's on at 2 and 5 every afternoon of the festival, apart from

103
00:04:04,665 --> 00:04:05,990
the first day.

104
00:04:05,990 --> 00:04:06,429
WOMAN:

105
00:04:06,429 --> 00:04:06,869
Lovely.

106
00:04:06,869 --> 00:04:09,944
I'm interested in all kinds of dancing,

107
00:04:09,944 --> 00:04:12,580
so I'm sure I'll enjoy that!

108
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:12,948
MAN:

109
00:04:12,948 --> 00:04:13,317
Mmm.

110
00:04:13,317 --> 00:04:14,790
I'm sure you will.

111
00:04:14,790 --> 00:04:15,125
WOMAN:

112
00:04:15,125 --> 00:04:19,480
And I'd really like to go to some concerts, if there are any.

113
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:20,016
MAN:

114
00:04:20,016 --> 00:04:22,162
Yes, there are several.

115
00:04:22,162 --> 00:04:24,308
Three performed by professionals,

116
00:04:24,308 --> 00:04:26,990
and one by local children.

117
00:04:26,990 --> 00:04:27,367
WOMAN:

118
00:04:27,367 --> 00:04:29,630
And where is it being held?

119
00:04:29,630 --> 00:04:30,092
MAN:

120
00:04:30,092 --> 00:04:31,941
It's in the library,

121
00:04:31,941 --> 00:04:34,251
which is in Park Street.

122
00:04:34,251 --> 00:04:38,410
On the 18th, at 6.30 in the evening.

123
00:04:38,410 --> 00:04:38,818
WOMAN:

124
00:04:38,818 --> 00:04:41,670
I presume I'll need tickets for that.

125
00:04:41,670 --> 00:04:42,098
MAN:

126
00:04:42,098 --> 00:04:42,526
Yes.

127
00:04:42,526 --> 00:04:44,239
You can book online,

128
00:04:44,239 --> 00:04:48,520
or you can buy them when you arrive in Kenton.

129
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:51,089
Either at the festival box office,

130
00:04:51,089 --> 00:04:55,370
or from any shops displaying our logo in the windows.

131
00:04:55,370 --> 00:04:55,722
WOMAN:

132
00:04:55,722 --> 00:04:56,073
Well.

133
00:04:56,073 --> 00:05:00,997
I think that'll keep me busy for the whole of my stay in Kenton.

134
00:05:00,997 --> 00:05:03,810
Thank you so much for all your help.

135
00:05:03,810 --> 00:05:04,257
MAN:

136
00:05:04,257 --> 00:05:05,150
You're welcome.

137
00:05:05,150 --> 00:05:07,830
I hope you enjoy your stay.

138
00:05:07,830 --> 00:05:08,558
WOMAN:

139
00:05:08,558 --> 00:05:10,012
Thank you.

140
00:05:10,012 --> 00:05:10,740
Goodbye.
